      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you, but it just feels like you're giving me the standard script. the \"new perspectives\" thing sounds good in theory but logically, if we look at the math of it, there's no real weight to any of it. if everything is eventually going to end and nothing we do actually leaves a permanent mark, then the value of being here vs not being here is basically zero. it's like a zero-sum game. why is one objectively better than the other? if the net outcome is just entropy anyway, choosing to stop",
